# Error messages. Codes and fix articles live in content/errors/errors.yaml (M1.9).

error-not-permitted = You don't have permission to do that.
error-unsupported-request = Selah couldn't do that. Try again, or restart Selah.
error-invalid-setting = That setting isn't allowed.
error-not-connected = Selah isn't connected yet. Wait a moment, then try again.
error-invalid-request = Selah couldn't read that request. Restart Selah if this keeps happening.
error-screen-not-connected = A screen is not connected. Check its cable, then try again.
error-screen-unplugged = A screen was unplugged. Plug it back in. Selah will use it again.
error-safe-mode = Selah started in safe mode. Some features are off.
error-help-not-found = Selah couldn't find that help article.
error-update-off = Update checks are off. Turn them on in Settings, then try again.
error-update-feed = Selah couldn't read the update address. Check the address and your internet, then try again.
error-update-verify = The update didn't download correctly, so Selah didn't install it. Try again later.
error-update-live = Something is on the screens. Clear them, then install the update.
error-update-install = Selah couldn't start the update. Try again, or install the new version from its Setup file.
